2026-09-02T14:37Z codex created

2026-09-02T19:47Z claude note SECOND ADAPTER LANDED, and the comparison it was filed to make produced four findings rather than a clean transport. The interface carries zoteus's architecture in four places. (1) Declaration.unsupported holds VERBS, so no adapter can say a MODE is absent; zotero-mcp has no combined mode at all (no fusion code anywhere in its source), meaning needs an optional extra the documented install does not pull, and exact ESCALATES through four strategies ending in semantic search with no switch to disable it -- disclosed in human-readable prose, not in a machine field, which makes R33's 'the mode selected MUST be the mode served' falsifiable on this target. The adapter answers served=False with a reason rather than a verdict, because an unreachable mode must not come back looking like zero hits. (2) An unsupported verb records no REASON, so 'has background work and exposes no control' and 'has no background work at all' land in one cell; here pause and resume are absent because in the default configuration the target does no unattended indexing whatsoever, which is architecturally opposite to a target hiding its control. (3) derived_state_roots presumes the target OWNS its state: three of this target's five roots are created by fastmcp, chromadb and onnxruntime at paths its own source never names, and the largest is a 167 MB model cache. zoteus does not have this problem because it vendors its embedder and pins the cache under its own data directory, so this is the sharpest place the interface assumes zoteus's shape. All five are declared as roots -- the field asks where state APPEARS -- and not_derived_state was rejected as the home, its documented purpose being user data and external configuration. (4) HOME is this target's only sandbox: the Chroma client and the update lock resolve the home directory directly, so its config-path option relocates part of one root out of five. Declared under process, and the constructor REFUSES the operator's own HOME rather than documenting the hazard. Two things the adapter's own measurement added: the ambient environment is part of the default configuration -- the target reads 28 variables including three hosted-provider keys, and upstream carries a comment about a key leaked from another tool silently rewriting the embedding config, so the adapter blanks all 28 because that is what makes 'default configuration' true rather than a non-default option; and the schema-refresh root is TIMING-DEPENDENT, written by an asyncio task, so a residue sweep that stops the process the moment its calls return will not see it. Nine deliberate control arms were fired against the committed tree, each on its intended guard. uninstall is not-offered on the evidence of a zero-hit grep across README, src and docs and the full 14-subcommand list; pip uninstall leaves all five roots and the harness does not delete them on the target's behalf. Both targets now run through one layer -- available() lists zoteus and zotero-mcp -- and the layer still holds no target's name.
